# Blender
*.blend1
*.blend2
*.blend@

# Build output. /build holds the two shippable artefacts, the .exe and the
# SCORM .zip; the loose web export lands in /build/scorm_build.
#
# Two empty files in there are tracked on purpose:
#   .gdignore  keeps Godot's scan - and so the next export's PCK - out of a
#              tree holding a 260 MB PCK, a 39 MB wasm and a 370 MB exe.
#   .gitkeep   keeps scorm_build/ existing on a fresh clone. Godot's exporter
#              does not create its target folder; it fails with "Target folder
#              does not exist" instead.
/build/*
!/build/.gdignore
!/build/scorm_build/
/build/scorm_build/*
!/build/scorm_build/.gitkeep
*.pck
*.exe
*.zip

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini

# Images LVR CPR.blend links from outside the project, which Godot therefore
# copies to the project root on every reimport - it cannot reference a path
# above res://. Only ArmsTexD is left: it belongs to an FPS arms pack nothing
# in the scene reaches, so it is untracked build scratch and the presets'
# exclude_filter keeps it out of the build too.
#
# The other root extractions - Gloves1 and T_Casualty_Body_color and
# ddp-100-large - are the only copy of those images and stay tracked. The
# T_Workers set used to land here as well, duplicating files already committed
# under textures/; that was fixed in the .blend by relinking those images to
# //textures/, so they are no longer extracted at all.
/LVR CPR_ArmsTexD.jpg
/LVR CPR_ArmsTexD.jpg.import
